cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  What binds a surrogate: a pre-registered falsification ladder for transfer
  to unseen adsorbent parameter sets in metal-organic framework
  water-adsorption columns
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Abdulhamid
    family-names: Batayhi
    email: abdulbatayhi@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/REPLACE-ME/ai-mof-cof-dynamics"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered falsification ladder testing seven candidate explanations
  for the error of surrogate models of metal-organic framework water-adsorption
  columns on adsorbents they have never seen: more training materials, more
  capacity, Kolmogorov-Arnold networks, a physics residual in the loss, operator
  learning, structural identification of the kinetic and equilibrium objects,
  and whether learning is needed at all. Each verdict is reported in words
  declared in advance; the results are in the accompanying manuscript. Includes
  a verified finite-difference reference solver, a calibrated cluster-robust
  inference protocol, a build that refuses any number not resolved from a
  results file, and a public correction ledger.
keywords:
  - metal-organic frameworks
  - atmospheric water harvesting
  - breakthrough curves
  - operator learning
  - reduced-order modelling
  - Kolmogorov n-width
  - physics-informed machine learning
  - negative results
  - pre-registration
license: MIT
